body:
This is for ChatBox 1.18.4 on a Mac M1 running MacOS 15.6.1.

Chat using provider as OpenAI chat completion API, model is gpt-5.2, thinking = heavy.  Web search with bing enabled. I asked it:

"XXX is a company that does YYY. What is their funding history? When did they start and how much have they raised, in what rounds, when, and from whom?"

ChatBox fired off a bunch of web queries until this error came back from OpenAI api:

{
  "error": {
    "message": "Invalid 'messages[28].tool_calls': array too long. Expected an array with maximum length 128, but got an array with length 146 instead.",
    "type": "invalid_request_error",
    "param": "messages[28].tool_calls",
    "code": "array_above_max_length"
  }
}

On Linux with Wayland compositors (tested on Hyprland), selecting text in Chatbox and copying it (Ctrl+C or right-click copy) then pasting into other applications causes those applications to hang or crash.

Note: the explicit copy buttons on messages and code blocks work fine - this only affects native text selection copy.

Steps to Reproduce

  1. Open Chatbox on Linux with a Wayland compositor
  2. Start a chat and get a response with some text
  3. Select some text in the response with your mouse
  4. Press Ctrl+C to copy
  5. Switch to another application (e.g. a text editor, terminal)
  6. Press Ctrl+V to paste
  7. The receiving application hangs or crashes

Probable Root Cause

Chatbox runs as an XWayland application. In XWayland, the clipboard is "live" - the source application (Chatbox/Electron) must keep serving clipboard requests from other apps for as long as the data is on the clipboard. When Wayland-native apps request the clipboard content, they communicate through the XWayland clipboard bridge to Electron. This is slow and unreliable, causing receiving apps to time out and crash.

Fix
Intercept the document copy event in the renderer and use wl-copy to hand the clipboard data off to the Wayland compositor's clipboard daemon immediately. This makes the data available system-wide without Electron needing to serve it.

  // renderer: intercept copy events
  document.addEventListener('copy', (e) => {
    const selectedText = window.getSelection()?.toString()
    if (selectedText) {
      e.preventDefault()
      electronAPI.invoke('clipboard-write', selectedText)
    }
  }, true)

  // main process: write via wl-copy
  ipcMain.handle('clipboard-write', (_event, text: string) => {
    if (process.platform === 'linux') {
      const proc = spawn('wl-copy', [], { stdio: ['pipe', 'ignore', 'ignore'] })
      proc.stdin.write(text)
      proc.stdin.end()
    }
  })

Environment

- OS: Arch Linux
- Desktop: Hyprland (Wayland)
- Chatbox version: 1.19.0

{
  "error": {
    "code": "400",
    "message": "Param Incorrect",
    "param": "The reasoning_content in the thinking mode must be passed back to the API.",
    "type": ""
  }
}

this is a bug for mimo-v2.5, please fix the bug
